! ============================================================
! 08a  Density fitting (RI-J): what it buys and what it costs
! ============================================================
! Pyrrole, PBE/cc-pVDZ, 100 basis functions.  Run BOTH files
! and compare.
!
! The Coulomb matrix J needs the four-index integrals (mn|ls),
! of which there are O(N^4).  Density fitting expands the
! density in an auxiliary basis, so J is built from three- and
! two-index integrals instead: O(N^3), with a much smaller
! prefactor.  Exchange cannot be fitted so cheaply, which is
! why RI-J helps pure functionals most and hybrids less.
!
! MEASURED HERE (1 core, reference BLAS):
!
!                        conventional     RI-J
!    2e-integrals (J,K)     11.72 s      0.09 s     130x
!    total wall             39.5  s      28.8 s     1.37x
!    total energy      -209.920245  -209.920442
!
! THREE THINGS THE TABLE TEACHES:
!
!  1. The Coulomb stage really does collapse -- 130-fold.  If
!     you only look at that line, RI looks miraculous.
!
!  2. The WALL TIME improves by 1.37x, not by 130x.  Once J is
!     free, the XC quadrature and the diagonalizations dominate,
!     and RI-J does nothing for either.  This is Amdahl's law
!     in one table: speeding up a stage can never save more
!     time than that stage was taking.  Always profile before
!     optimizing -- %print_time is there for exactly this.
!
!  3. The energy changes by 2.0e-4 Ha = 0.12 kcal/mol, about
!     20 uHa per atom.  That is the accuracy class of the
!     def2-universal-JFIT auxiliary basis, and it is a
!     SYSTEMATIC offset, not noise: it largely cancels in
!     energy differences between similar structures, which is
!     why RI-J is safe for geometries and reaction energies
!     and less so for a single absolute number.
!
! %ri_check on prints a fitted-vs-exact J diagnostic, but it
! builds the exact J by the O(N^4) route to do so -- it costs
! about as much as the conventional run it is meant to replace.
! Use it to validate, never in a timing measurement.
!
! THIS FILE: conventional, no fitting.
%method  PBE
%basis   cc-pVDZ
%job     energy
%grid    fine
%print_time
%charge  0
%mult    1

%geo
 C   -0.71390000    1.11450000    0.00000000
 C    0.71390000    1.11450000    0.00000000
 C    1.12490000   -0.20860000    0.00000000
 C   -1.12490000   -0.20860000    0.00000000
 N    0.00000000   -1.00250000    0.00000000
 H   -1.36930000    1.97440000    0.00000000
 H    1.36930000    1.97440000    0.00000000
 H    2.13120000   -0.59440000    0.00000000
 H   -2.13120000   -0.59440000    0.00000000
 H    0.00000000   -2.01120000    0.00000000
